{"annotationDigest":"sha256:5c459f8dbe9dd5d11b7a35d9c3a744f14ec471a1021a9ada1b9cf99a18d3af01","annotationId":"rann-768b15d107a12125c22180b1400ce91c","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-04T09:28:29Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":0,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":3,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"ready"},"findings":[{"detail":"`test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh` has no functions; it runs 9 top-level rows against the real script with a stub selector. Line 5 `# Verifies: SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ, SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y` (our proof work) gives it a file-level trace. review.scope flags the unit `behaviour_without_intent` / `exact_file_trace` / `weak_mapping`, but `specGapCandidates` is empty. Head cc710e11 adds row 128-139: `photo.webm` and its hard link `cover.webm` in one root must give two rows. Re-run locally this round with bfs (a GNU-compatible find, not GNU find): at cc710e11 all 9 rows pass; with the 03e6af6a script the first 8 pass and the hard-link row fails (only `cover.webm` offered); with the baseline script the first row fails (no file offered under a link root). The menu-shell catch-all runs it as its own JUnit testcase (proof.yaml:216), and review.tests records it as passed.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh","kind":"file","line":128},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh","kind":"file","line":5},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"proof.yaml","kind":"file","line":216}],"severity":"info","title":"The PR's test traces at file level, and its new hard-link row fails on the previous head","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not